The CA bundle at /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt holds the root
certificates of the Mozilla CA program. The curl project extracts them
from Mozilla's certdata.txt and publishes them at
https://curl.se/docs/caextract.html. The header of the bundle names
the date of the certificate data.

Mozilla's certdata.txt is subject to the Mozilla Public License,
version 2.0. The bundle is a PEM file, which is its own source form.
A copy of the license is at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
